    <DataNode elementId="AT5G20990-MONOMER" textLabel="AT5G20990-MONOMER" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="1EAV" dataSource="pdb" />
      <Graphics centerX="150" centerY="215" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="THE-ARABIDOPSIS-INFORMATION-RESOURCE, hartmut">The insertion of molybdenum (Mo) into molybdopterin (MPT) generating the dioxyo form of molybdenum cofactor (moco) is catalyzed in plants by the two-domain protein Cnx1 |CITS: [ 8528286]|. The C-terminus of the enzyme (Cnx1G) first binds molybdopterin and forms the adenylated intermediate (MPT-AMP). Molybdopterin-AMP serves as matrix for the insertion of Mo catalyzed by the N-terminus of the enzyme (Cnx1E) |CITS: [16669776]|. This multifunctional enzyme in plants |CITS: [11148290]| |CITS: [16367968]| is homologues to the mammalian gephyrin |CITS: [ 9990024]| and two monofunctional proteins in &lt;i&gt;E. coli&lt;/i&gt; (MoeA, MogA) |CITS: [1587808]| catalyzing the same step(s) in moco biosynthesis in those organisms.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT5G20990-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Araport" value="AT5G20990.1" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Pdb" value="1EAV" />
